  === Complete Solutions

  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Farming and mining are primary industry, manufacturing is secondary, and warehousing is a commercial service.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Goods start at the producer and end at the consumer; the middlemen arrange the passage.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The sleeping partner supplies capital and shares profit without managing. A limited partner also limits his liability, which is a separate feature.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Democratic control is the defining rule, whatever the capital contributed.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Storage moves the good through time to when it is wanted, which is time utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    One owner means one fortune at risk and one purse to draw on.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    It is used by charities and clubs: no share capital, and members guarantee a small amount.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Incorporation normally brings limited liability; unlimited liability is the mark of the unincorporated business.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The fixed, prior dividend is what the preference shareholder buys with his lower upside.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    It has no share capital; the state provides the funds and appoints the board.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Free transferability is what makes a quotation meaningful.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The wholesaler buys in shiploads and sells in lorry loads; the retailer buys in lorry loads and sells in units.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Self-service with payment at the exit is the operating model.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The wholesaler's margin is saved, but his storage and credit functions must be taken on.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    25% of 8,000 is 2,000, so the invoice price is 6,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Margin is profit over selling price: cost is 80% of 4,500 = 3,600.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Both divide larger lots into smaller ones; the difference is the customer they serve.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Services — freight, insurance, tourism, banking — leave no visible cargo.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Double entry means the accounts balance even when trade does not; the deficit is financed, not erased.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The duty raises the import price, so local producers can compete and the state collects revenue.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Whoever holds the endorsed bill of lading can claim the goods.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The exporter (drawer) orders the importer (drawee) to pay at sight or on a stated date.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    1,200 − 1,050 = 150 in favour of exports, so a surplus.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    A licence restricts without taxing; the others are duties.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Storage holds goods until the moment of demand.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Indemnity caps recovery at the actual loss; contribution then divides that loss between insurers.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    4 × (5 ÷ 10) = 2, so the claim is ₦2m. Under-insurance shares the loss.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Banks treat cheques over six months old as stale and return them.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Pipelines carry fluids continuously at the lowest cost per unit.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    It shifts the demand curve toward the advertised brand.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The passbook and the interest are the marks of the savings account.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Stock, debtors, cash and bank balances are the standard current assets.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
